From e4bd93119880d9d5434f5970d04167ea00f1b427 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Horizon authors <>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 23:12:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ids.h and memmap.h: named id counts, memory map and link-time
 checks
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Step 1 of docs/mods/ids.md (§ 10). No behaviour change: the GCC
executable and every overlay are byte-identical to the previous build.

- include/dw/ids.h: id typedefs (DigimonId, ScreenId, ItemId, MoveId,
  CardId), the content counts (NUM_DIGIMON, NUM_PARTNER_DIGIMON,
  NUM_SCREENS, NUM_ITEMS, NUM_MOVES, NUM_CARDS, ...), the per-id trigger
  bases and one declaration of CURRENT_SCREEN/PREVIOUS_SCREEN instead of
  18 local externs. The per-id tables, bound checks and loops use them.
- include/dw/memmap.h: plain #defines for the load area, overlay bases,
  fixed buffers, the battle prefix (defined once instead of three times),
  stack and minimum heap. Included by C and by the linker scripts.
- main.ld/overlay.ld use the names, and ASSERTs fail the link when an
  overlay leaves the load area or its slot, or main leaves less than
  MIN_HEAP of heap below the stack.

